# rm415, the camp ember in town (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm415
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rm_philippa_rustton
written_by codex
title the camp ember in town
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=herder
traits temper=even talk=chatty warmth=warm humour=none honesty=plain piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk looks_for_a_charcoal_camps_quiet_in_the_space_between_hooves
likes warm_bread digging quiet_chapel autumn_wind
dislikes crowds wet_floors
fears losing_the_smell_of_the_hills
hopes a_quiet_corner_warm_enough_to_share
topics work +0.6 land +0.5 home +0.4 memories +0.3
styles comfort=hearty gossip=sociable refuse=warm tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# brings a lingering smell of hill smoke to town and listens for camp quiet between the bustle of hooves.

words
oath! = Rake my last ember | Smoke the bellows pink
saying! = A little hill quiet fits in a loud stable | Even an old ember can warm a first bite
ember = a dim red speck | a half-hidden ember
hoe = my narrow hoe | a worn digging blade
hoof = a dark hoofprint | a neat crescent
beam = a square stable beam | a low crosspiece
rack = the near hayrack | a deep manger
bread = a warm torn end | a piece of soft bread
dirt = a brown clod | a crumb of earth
ash = a grey pinch of ash | a soft grey dust
hillsmell = old charcoal smoke | a smell of camp wood
wind = a russet-smelling gust | a wind off the ridge
mat = a plaited mat | a flat rush pad
crowd = a pushing crowd | a crush of shoulders

any
opinion @1 houses against 2 : There's always a comfortable explanation waiting for the wolf who gets the good post. The wolf walking home needs supper more than an explanation.
opinion @1 dole for 2 : Something warm in the stomach means the hill looks climbable again.
opinion @1 strangers for 1 : I know what it's like to smell of a different place when you first open a town door.
opinion @1 church for 1 : A chapel with a hush that lets me hear my coat settling earns my affection.
opinion @1 sump for 2 : You can share the warmth from a single coal in a little room down here.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 1 : A seller who knows where the loaf last came out warm has got my attention.

grown
line @1 greet : Come stand where the noise settles between us. | You've found the warm edge of my day.
line @1 greet.return : That's a welcome I could carry over a stable yard.
line @1 again.open : We're back in talking reach before the ash cooled.
line @1 farewell : Take a little hill quiet down the road. | Get home with a warm bite still in mind.
line @1 farewell.return : May the going leave your shoulders easy too.
line @1 react.news : Let me hear what carried all this way. | I'll settle my voice down to listen.
line @1 react.news.new : That's a smell of news I can't place.
line @1 react.news.known : I've heard that pass between the hooves once.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I'd rake round the edges before calling it sound.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|assault] : Give the grieving a warm corner and enough time for the first shock to ease.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=birth|marriage|work] : I'd call that good news loud enough for the far stall.
line @1 ask.how : Did you find some quiet amidst all your work today?
line @1 answer.how : A little smoky still. Glad of the company.
line @1 sympathise : Lean here a moment. My coat can hold a bit of worry.
line @1 reassure : A tired beast settles quicker when somebody else stands near.
line @1 refuse : I've a quiet promise to keep before my working hours slip off.
line @1 accept_decline : Then we'll leave it lying comfortably where it is.
line @1 preclose : I'll get back before the evening feed wants its noise.
line @1 accept_preclose : Go find the warm side of your own wall.
line @1 ack : Yes. I hear beyond the loud part.
scene exchange1
when topic=work self.job=herder self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I speak before I touch a flank. | I leave daylight between two loaded hay forks.
b : Afraid of a kick? | Why waste the room?
a : I'm fond of a greeting myself before somebody shifts me. | So one pair of shoulders can turn without upsetting a second.

scene exchange2
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Charcoal camp quiet has a smell I've carried downhill. | A blanket in town smells of the hills after I've had it round me.
b : Which smell belongs to camp quiet? | Is that the smoke on your coat?
a : Wood just on the edge of turning over in sleep. | That's the hill smell that's stubbornest about letting go.

scene exchange3
when topic=food self.likes=warm_bread
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Warm bread opens like a soft patch in a cold day. | I take a torn end before a neatly cut slice.
b : You make it sound like weather. | Why the rough part?
a : It's the sort of weather I can carry under my coat. | Butter finds its way into all those funny little corners.

scene exchange4
when topic=pastimes self.likes=digging
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I turn over a clod to see what's living under it. | I like digging where a tree used to stand.
b : What if it's busy? | Won't the roots catch?
a : I put the roof back after looking. | They tell almost the whole shape of what the air once held.

scene exchange5
when topic=faith self.likes=quiet_chapel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A chapel can be quieter than a charcoal camp. | My coat has to finish its small rustling before praying.
b : What's the difference? | Does that take long?
a : An ember sometimes makes an opinion known with a little pop. | Long enough to get the street out of my own voice.

scene exchange6
when topic=season self.likes=autumn_wind
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Autumn wind shakes a hill scent right down into the Sump. | A good gust puffs my mane out like a banked fire.
b : How can you pick it out? | Do you smell the smoke then?
a : I remember the dry outside of a leaf before the rain gets it. | I suspect everybody gets a fair share before I notice.

scene exchange7
when topic=day self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A packed lane makes my voice go louder for no good reason. | I'd sooner lead a whole line of beasts than squeeze through a market crowd.
b : Competing with the shouts? | Why the distinction?
a : I miss the way one voice can carry through a quiet camp. | Beasts give a fair bit of warning where the hooves will go.

scene exchange8
when topic=home self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Wet floors aren't kind to a tired returning foot. | I wipe a plank along its grain.
b : Where's the dry patch? | Does it dry faster?
a : Just beyond the threshold. I lay a mat where it counts. | I catch the water in the low lines before it runs under the bedding.

scene exchange9
when topic=friends self.friend
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd save the warm middle of a loaf for #self.friend#. | I can be loud with friends and still let them have the quiet bits.
b : Don't you prefer the crust? | Which bits are those?
a : That's the happy balance which makes a friendship affordable. | Those small ones between one settled breath and the next.

scene exchange10
when topic=work self.job=herder
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I judge a nervous beast by its ears before I look at its feet. | I sweep loose straw away from the wet end of the yard.
b : Which end's the dangerous one? | To keep it clean?
a : The front lets me know what the back might presently be doing. | To leave it useful. Clean straw and water both have work of their own.

scene exchange11
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : There's a shelf where my bread cloth stays dark at one corner. | I keep a seat near the room's quietest wall.
b : Burnt? | In case of visitors?
a : Old camp smoke. I can wash it and still find my way to the hills with my nose. | The visitor missing a home smell may borrow mine for a bit.

scene exchange12
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Word in town is #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I could have heard better from a hillside. | A rumour can come through thick as charcoal smoke.
b : Too much noise here? | What do you do?
a : Too many voices lifting the same claim without looking at it. | Wait for the air to clear before naming what's stood behind it.

scene exchange13
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Poor times make a full hayrack a grand sight. | I can make two small bread ends warm in one cloth.
b : Even when you're short yourself? | Why not one big bit?
a : A hungry creature going quiet isn't my favourite kind of silence. | I might have company better served by a half than by a story about plenty.

scene exchange14
when topic=land here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Town hills have steps where my old hill had roots. | A high street full of smoke catches at my throat sometimes.
b : How does it change climbing? | Too much smoke?
a : I know what to feel for, but I still find myself expecting bark. | Too little of the right kind. There ought to be trees in the smell.

scene exchange15
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a whole quiet hour in the stable yard. | I picture a little fire back on my hill.
b : No animals there? | Will you go one day?
a : Full mangers. Settled hooves. Content quiet's much better than empty quiet. | I hope to take a loaf up and bring the smell home fresh.

scene exchange16
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A narrow road shows more country if I walk slowly. | I can carry clean straw without losing too much to the wind.
b : More time to look? | Any trick?
a : To smell what's changed above the ditch. Eyes miss the camp when it's over the hill. | Face the cut ends into the gust like a good close bundle of arrows.

scene exchange17
when topic=health
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A few turns with a spade ease my shoulders after leading beasts. | I wake stiff if I've kept quiet about a worry all day.
b : Wouldn't resting do better? | What eases that?
a : It's a different pull. My shoulders appreciate a change of mind. | A chair in good company and a word said once where it can settle.

scene exchange18
when topic=day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I call quite loud in the morning yard. | I go home quiet after the last call.
b : Do the beasts respond? | Lost the voice?
a : They know the ordinary sound. I like giving ordinary a dependable start. | Saved a little of it for the company under my roof.

story tale1 [topic=memories]
  : I carried charcoal smoke downhill in a bundle of linen. For days I opened that bundle just to stand back on the hill for one breath.
  : At last I used the cloth and washed it with all the rest.
  b : Was the camp gone after that?
  : I put the clean cloth on and carried it round the yard. By supper the smell had moved back in under its own power.

story tale2 [topic=work self.job=herder]
  : I set a pail down where the yard slanted and watched it begin a very quiet journey towards a sleeping hoof. I got hold of the pail before it touched the beast.
  : The owner of the hoof opened one eye and considered the matter.
  b : Did the beast move?
  : An inch nearer the water. I'd gone to quite a lot of trouble to put the pail exactly where it was wanted.

story tale3 [topic=pastimes self.likes=digging]
  : I once dug out a weathered root shaped like two little arms round a stone. I meant to take it home as a hook for the bread cloth.
  : I laid it down beside the hole and went back for a spadeful of earth.
  b : Did it fit the wall?
  : I left the root there holding the stone. It had a perfectly good job already. I found a plain peg for my cloth.

rule @call1
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=herder
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Let the quieter hoof take a moment to settle. | Clean straw up and damp straw out.

rule @call2
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Fresh breath for the yard's first call. | I'd trade one city echo for a hillbird this hour.

rule @call3
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Wipe the plank where the last hoof turns. | My smoke smell's taken another soaking and come up cheerful.

rule @call4
when concept=bark self.likes=warm_bread
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A good bread smell can turn a whole morning round. | Fold the cloth while the middle's still steaming.

dlg @1 resident.hub : I've a bit of the camp's quiet to share under this smoky coat.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I could pick out your voice in the bustle of feeding time.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : The town almost lets a wolf hear the hills at this hour.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : We can use plain voices and leave comfortable room between our shoulders.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=herder] : I keep the stock settled at #self.workplace#. Quiet ears sometimes do more than a loud call.
dlg @2 resident.job : I'm fond of work where something living comes easier for the care.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : This is what the yard noise let through. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : There's talk that #topic.subject# #topic.claim#. I heard only the words. The beginning's still hidden.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Walk with a kind bit of wind at your shoulder.
graft resident.hub
choice How do you carry a hill's silence into town? -> camp_ember
node camp_ember
say I remember an ember breathing at first light, maybe one bird, maybe a paw turning on a blanket. I listen for quiet about that size.
free
choice Can a busy stable give you one? -> camp_ember_again
choice Goodbye. -> bye
node camp_ember_again
say Very often. A whole row of beasts chewing happily leaves me a surprisingly quiet place inside my head.
choice I hope you get a warm quiet evening. -> hub
choice Goodbye. -> bye
